        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/r2SU7qp8y9CptckagPjFpwD1xsI=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/30578-filet-mignon-with-rich-balsamic-glaze-VAT-step-02-7412f764cb39439db3b73e2dd6558759.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/30578/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat a nonstick skillet over medium-high heat. Sear steaks in the hot pan until browned, about 1 minute per side.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/pC6QiUFqTwy9FwUGfGBHtCvzjFM=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/30578-filet-mignon-with-rich-balsamic-glaze-VAT-step-03-803ce89bb7184ea6814805c97a27987e.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/30578/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reduce heat to medium-low, and pour in balsamic vinegar and red wine. Cover and cook for 4 minutes. Flip steaks and baste with sauce; cover and cook for 4 minutes longer.",
